BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Society of Professional Journalists": "http://www.eventbrite.com/e/world-press-freedom-day-reception-tickets-1987397248670?aff=oddtdtcreator"}
X-SOURCE-ID:spj
X-SOURCE:Society of Professional Journalists
DTSTAMP:20170606T23231Z
UID:Rsd4Z2Vzot-8223722574@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T183000
SUMMARY:World Press Freedom Day Reception at the National Press Club
URL:http://www.eventbrite.com/e/world-press-freedom-day-reception-tickets-1987397248670?aff=oddtdtcreator
DESCRIPTION:Join us in recognition of World Press Freedom Day: A moment to celebrate the essential role of a free press and to stand in clear-eyed solidarity with journalists around the world.

This year\, we come together with both pride and urgency.

Across the globe and here at home\, journalists are doing extraordinary work under increasing pressure -- facing threats\, arrests\, restrictions\, and a rapidly shifting information landscape. Yet\, every day\, they continue to report\, investigate\, and inform their communities with courage and integrity.

This reception is an opportunity to pause and recognize that work -- to connect with colleagues\, partners\, and advocates committed to press freedom -- and to reaffirm our shared responsibility to support and protect it. 

The evening will feature brief remarks\, community\, and conversation\, highlighting both the challenges ahead and the enduring strength of a free and independent press. We’ll also introduce our 2026 Press Freedom Fellow Cohort\, journalists who have experienced obstacles but who persist in their pursuit of journalism. 


LOCATION:National Press Building\, Washington\, DC\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Society of Professional Journalists": "http://calendar.spjnetwork.org/displayevent.php?e=1oCZ107DJK-8224845011"}
X-SOURCE-ID:spj
X-SOURCE:Society of Professional Journalists
DTSTAMP:20170606T23232Z
UID:1oCZ107DJK-8224845011@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T113000
SUMMARY:Staying Safe in the Field 
URL:http://calendar.spjnetwork.org/displayevent.php?e=1oCZ107DJK-8224845011
DESCRIPTION:Join the SPJ Georgia Pro Chapter for part 2 of their “Safety & Security for Journalists” workshop series -- Staying Safe in the Field.

This in-person\, hands-on\, interactive training will give you practical tips on physical safety -- whether you’re reporting on conflicts and civil unrest\, working the general assignment beat or editing in the newsroom.

Our instructor brings 20+ years of combined experience in public safety and corporate security and will cover situational awareness\, active attacker response\, first aid basics and protest & field safety.

Pastries and coffee will be served. Parking is free. 

This event is for SPJ members only. RSVP is required at spjgeorgia@gmail.com

LOCATION:Georgia Public Broadcasting\, Atlanta\, GA
END:VEVENT
